to be silent or afraid.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It was a decision I knew that was right for me.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Parents have a lot more power than you think. You have power in numbers. I'm tell you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: My daughter was sexually assaulted at the end of school. I went to the school board meeting to see what was going on. The next thing I know, I'm tackled to the ground.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: My son was viciously taken from me, burnt alive in the garbage. And no mother should have to deal with that.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Never forgot Demetrius, not one day since last year. And it's a $15,000 reward. It's $20,000 now.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What do you pray for when you pray for this country?\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Peace. Really, peace.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Back with me now is Raymond Arroyo.\par \par \uc2 I love this two shot. I don't know why I think this is fun.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Smile! Do we have it?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Go to the edge. Go to the edge.\par \par \uc2 The ACLU used to care about the rights of the accused.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You threw me down in such a cruel fashion. Heartless.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: My hand slipped a little bit.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You pushed me.\par \par \uc2 (MUSIC)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Happy Mardi Gras. Is this unbelievable? Look at this crowd, Laura.\par \par \uc2 Wait, is there --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh. Raymond knows that if a see a bug, I can't help but scream. I officially hate you. I am so embarrassed.\par \par \uc2 I'm here with Raymond Arroyo for our watch party, with party favors being handed out.\par \par \uc2 What do you have say to America from Oxford, Mississippi?\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Hotty Toddy.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Hotty Toddy.\par \par \uc2 (APPLAUSE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I can't believe it's been four years. Raymond, is that not scary? It seems literally like yesterday. If you told me we're on the air for two years, I would say, yes, two years. Four years?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: It's a total blur. But Laura, I kept thinking of Paris, Normandy, those great moments, being at that historic moment, the 75th anniversary of Normandy. But the moment that stuck out to me that we don't have, sadly, on video, is when you returned to the studio and were locked in the bathroom just moments before showtime, we thought we would have to send a demolition crew in to remove the door. It's those moments that live strongest in my heart.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I wouldn't be surprised if Sam (ph) somehow did get that on video. I know by the time the fifth anniversary rolls around, Tommy (ph) and Sam (ph) will say, by the way, we did have a small camera as you emerged from the bathroom.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Security cam.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, coming up. This was just a few weeks ago because we opened up our studio again in Washington. And it was a brand new latch. And something happened, the latch wouldn't open. And I tried to pry it open with a Lysol can and a plunger, and it didn't work.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes, I heard you were ready to slip under the wall there.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: We are always going to persevere to get on the air every night. Tommy (ph), Sam (ph), David (ph), Michael (ph), I will miss people. Mike we have multiple Mikes. Everyone, Elisa (ph) is on maternity leave. But we have so many great people.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Jessica (ph).\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Jessica (ph), who else am I missing? This is like the Academy. It's the Academy Awards. There's going to be a hook taken. But everyone knows how important they are on this show. And Raymond, you have been integral to keeping me laughing and informed.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Thank you for making me a part of the fun. It's been a joy.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Absolutely fun every night. We love everyone