ents should resist this. They will become folk heroes if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's team tries to throw them in prison for opposing their liberal agenda. And Dana, I don't know if you saw Andy McCarthy today --\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I did.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: -- in the National Review -- he's got a great piece.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: One of the lines from the \uc2 FBI\uc2  -- this is their mantra. Process is the penalty. So, what they do is they threaten these federal investigations, very torturous and expensive, they threaten indictments, which can ruin your life, and what that does is that she'll speech. So, they are basically extorting silence from their political opponents. And no one is ever going to stop them unless parents stand up.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Is there any role here for the \uc2 FBI\uc2 ?\par \par \uc2 JEANINE PIRRO, FOX NEWS HOST: Absolutely not. This is something if there's a problem, you call the local police, you call the sheriff department, you call the D.A. The last person you want to call is the \uc2 FBI\uc2  because we already know how they botched this, whether it's the Nassar case from the Olympics, or whether it was the Parkland school shootings, or I could go on and on, the Epstein case, and on and on.\par \par \uc2 They have no role in this. The \uc2 FBI\uc2  likes to get involved where they get a lot of headlines.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Right.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But let's focus more on the issue. What is important here? What's important here are parents have a fundamental right to decide what is going to be in their child's education. These are not people who don't have a say. It's their children, not the state's children.\par \par \uc2 And what's so incredible about all of this is that we've got little Johnny who is coming home from school, and Johnny says he's getting yelled at in class. He's six years old, he wears glasses. And when he pulls down his mask when his glasses fogged up, a teacher yelled at him to put his mask back up.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: And we've got kids like this all over the country who are spending more time cleaning their desk than they are actually learning anything. And then we have the issue of, you know, other kids who are now being put in -- and another kid in advanced algebra when last year she didn't even learn fundamental algebra because the teachers weren't even -- weren't even in school.\par \par \uc2 I think the teachers are the last people that Americans see as victims in this case. If anything, they were made rich during a pandemic. They didn't want to come to work, and now they want to yell at our children. And there was a time where they were celebrities.\par \par \uc2 Now, kids see their teachers on the streets and teachers don't recognize them because they're all masked up.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: They don't even know who their students are. It is absolutely not the role of the feds.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Jessica, is it possible to be charitable to the White House and the DOJ, that this is yet another example of them not explaining something while dumb I cannot explain something well, sending out a memo, and then not actually dealing with the communications fall out?\par \par \uc2 JESSICA TARLOV, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: It's totally feasible. And to pick up on something that Jesse said, you know, use the word peaceful which is critical to the first amendment and understanding of how these meetings should go. We all realize that even if you disagree with someone you should treat people with respect. You shouldn't get in their faces.\par \par \uc2 There's video of people, of teachers and school board members being accosted on the street. It's my impression, just understanding, you know, President Biden and the people who work for him, \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , they don't seem like irrational people that they are going to be talking about folks who are taking this to an inappropriate level versus just someone who is saying excuse me, I don't agree with this but at a curriculum.\par \par \uc2 And most parents, I think, should understand that the mass mandates are not coming from the teachers themselves. That's coming from the higher on upstairs.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: But the \uc2 FBI\uc2  involvement.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: the \uc2 FBI\uc2  involvement doesn't seem to make a ton of sense. And it also might be one of those things that we get upset about for a few weeks. It never comes to fruition. It was kind an aside thing that \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2  did comment on because --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Maybe he got a call from the White House and he was like fine, I will put out the memo. But anyway, they did it and he's got a lot of attention. And a lot of people are mad and upset and they were mad before. But just this week, President Biden when he asked about the harassment Kyrsten Sinema, the senator from Arizona when followed into the bathroom, he said, it's part of the process.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: But she was basically like saying, you know, this happens to everybody and it's OK.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's not OK. Kiersten Powers, she's at CNN, she said, had this tweet. Which is worse, your grandparents being deported or being followed into a bathroom because you refused to stop and listen by people desperate for your help? This is not a trick question.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Wow.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: And then I think when people called her on this, she said, hey look, you know, if Kyrsten didn't want to be bothered in the bathroom, she shouldn't have gone to the bathroom. That's kind of like saying you asked for it. This is part of two trends. Biden is OK with that, but they are not OK with hypothetical crimes.\par \par \uc2 What that person did in the bathroom could be construed as a crime coming with a camera and filming somebody.\par \par \uc2 WAT