e knew about the French being displaced --\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Not when he said --\par \par \uc2 PSAKI: Let me finish.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: -- literally have not been aware.\par \par \uc2 PSAKI: Peter, I would encourage you to ask \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  specifically about the context of his comments, the president and the former secretary are also good friends. He relies on his counsel, as he does with many numbers of his national security team. But that's certainly is not what he was intending to convey.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 TARLOV (on camera): So, Greg, what I thought was interesting about this, first of all, that obviously that's not what she wanted to be talking about. But \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  comes from Kerry world, she doesn't come from Biden world. So, what did you think of her defense?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Well, she had no defense. She had -- that's why she had a spin. I think the spinning will be \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  wasn't aware of it, so again, it's not his fault.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Right.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: So now, his profound ignorance and possible confusion in this job, it's a shield against criticism. hey, it's grandpa Joe, he didn't know. I think that the Dems like it this way. The less he knows the better. Because he really was elected to be kind of a shell for a whole other group of Democrats, right? He was the Trojan horse. It raises the question, what else does Joe not know, and when did he not know it? Get that? No?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Got it.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: She just didn't like it.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: She just didn't like it.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: No.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: When did he not know and when did he not know it?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: He never knew.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: He never know!\par \par \uc2 PERINO: That's the funny part.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That's been his M.O., plausible deniability.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Exactly.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Right? And even the French know. I think when Kerry said Biden didn't really get it, the French said, you know, you're right, he probably didn't get it. And he takes the sting out of them losing that deal. And you know \uc2 John Kerry\uc2  thought he should have been president. You know, Kerry --\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: -- was in the Senate with \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 . \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was always a joke in the Senate. Kerry thinks like listen, this guy just does it now here and it slipped and he did throw him under the yacht.\par \par \uc2 But this is the biggest alliance or military development in the pacific for decades, this new alliance we have with the Australians and the British against the Chinese. If Biden didn't know about that and the implications about that, that is pretty scary we not only gave the Australian submarines, we gave them mid-range missiles that can hit the Chinese mainland, hit all their shipping lanes, and China can't do anything about it. They're out of range.\par \par \uc2 So, the Chinese are humiliated, they're panicking and that's why they're lashing out against Taiwan to prop up the regime domestically, but you know, they're up, you know, what's creek.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: You know, Jessica, can I repeat my joke again so it gets clipped and people see how brilliant it is. I think it raises a question what does Joe not know and when did he not know it?\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: Do you like it now, Judge?\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Yes, it works.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: OK, thank you.\par \par \uc2 TARLOV: On that note, ahead, new calls for censorship in the fallout from the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  whistleblower.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Liberals using the fallout from the \uc2 Facebook\uc2  whistleblower to call for censorship. Journalist Glenn Greenwald says the controversy is being embraced by Democrats and media who do not want to weaken \uc2 Facebook\uc2  but instead commandeer its power to censor. And CNN's Don Lemon is proving his point.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DON LEMON, ANCHOR, CNN: It allows lies to be spread unchecked. So, if we say something on this network that is not true, there are repercussions and ramifications, right? We face the consequences. If you do that on social media, there are no consequences. What we post on social media, what is posted on social media should be true so. And if it's not true, it should be taken --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: So, what if it's -- what if it's --\par \par \uc2 LEMON: Take it down. If it's not true, take it down. If it's not true, don't allow people to put it up there. Have them face consequences.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Journalists.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: OK, Greg, who decides what's true and what isn't?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Yes, that's idiotic.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Who is the arbiter --\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: Don Lemon.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: This is -- this is just -- I mean, it's amazing. Lemon on THE FIVE though. We just gave him the biggest audience in his career. He would have to do 70 shows in a row to get the number of eyeballs that just saw him. This is the -- they're -- you know, the Republicans and Democrats both have problems with \uc2 Facebook\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The Republicans look at \uc2 Facebook\uc2  as something that may be contributing to a moral decline like alcohol and drugs, right? These are things that are bad for kids and maybe we should create an age limit. Like, for cigarettes and alcohol, there's a certain age limit to get on social media but not making it illegal.\par \par \uc2 This is different. What he's talking about is eliminating discourse. He's going to be the decider on what's true and what's false. It's about controlling the narrative. It has nothing to do with a moral idea, it has nothing to do with truth, it has to do with politics and political power.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: But Dana, essentially, aren't they eliminating all opinion because they can say that your opinion is based upon a fact that is not accurate in their minds?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Well, remember that the people on the right have been frustrated with \uc2 Facebook\uc2  for a while because of claims of censorship and bias, OK.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: Right.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: But the left hates \uc2 Facebook\uc2  for a couple of reasons. One, Republicans are actually more successful on \uc2 Facebook\uc2  than they are in reaching audiences. If you look at the top ten pages, you'll find people -- Fox News there, Dan Bongino, you'll see \uc2 Ben Shapiro\uc2  and others.\par \par \uc2 OK, so the left hates \uc2 Facebook\uc2 . And for as much as the Right hates \uc2 Facebook\uc2 , the left hates it so much more. They can't control it. And you -- it was very weird to watch last night how like the bat signal had gone out and everyone in the media had the exact same language. It's all about the whistleblower. It turns out though she's got some connections with the Democratic Party or long-term Democrats that have like helped her out on this whole thing.\par \par \uc2 I'm just -- I'm skeptical of the whole thing. I'm not saying that \uc2 Facebook\uc2  doesn't need to be regulated. Maybe they do. I'm just thinking that this whole thing to me seemed a little bit strange.\par \par \uc2 PIRRO: You know, in terms of -- Jesse, in terms of Don Lemon saying there has to be consequences, I love when he said, if we at CNN do something on the network that's not true, we face consequences. I'm thinking Chris Cuomo, Jeffrey Toobin. Are there consequences at CNN?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: I mean, they push the Russia hoax for how long? Were there consequences for that? No. And Dana is right. This smells like a setup to me. It reminds me of the Christine Blasey Ford, Ukraine whistleblower phone call. All of a sudden, this woman, after photocopying a bunch of documents and she was in charge of nuking the \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2  laptop thing fro