 (voice-over): The two Dems not onboard: \uc2 Joe Manchin\uc2 , who was greeted at his House vote by chi (PH) activists.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We all love our state too much to see a go by the wayside.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: And Kyrsten Sinema, hounded by protesters and a lady's room.\par \par \uc2 She now says, "It is the duty of elected leaders to avoid fostering an environment in which honestly-held policy disagreements serve as the basis for vitriol -- raising the temperature in political rhetoric and creating a permission structure for unacceptable behavior."\par \par \uc2 Fox News asked the president about these progressive protesters?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Do you think that those tactics are crossing a line?\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I don't think they're appropriate tactics, but it happens to everybody from -- the only people it doesn't happen to are people who have Secret Service standing around them. So, it's part of the process.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (on camera): Part of the process. And since President Biden is an expert on the process, I asked his Press Secretary \uc2 Jen Psaki\uc2  today if that means that he has ever been chased into a restroom by activists? She didn't answer that part but did reiterate they think that behavior in the restroom with Senator Sinema is unacceptable.\par \par \uc2 However, she reiterated the president's support for the fundamental right to protest. Bret?\par \par \uc2 Well, have Senator Sinema or Manchin reacted to President Biden's remark about the efforts to go after them part of the process?\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Not since President Biden made that comment late this morning. And we have laid eyes on them. Senator Manchin is already back on the Hill. He talks about some policy things and his thoughts on infrastructure. Didn't mention the Chi (PH) activists.\par \par \uc2 Senator Sinema, meanwhile, there is some footage bubbling up on social media in the last few minutes, arriving at Washington Reagan National Airport, hounded by protesters.\par \par \uc2 She didn't say anything, but they're obviously not done with her yet. Part of the process, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Peter Doocy live in the North Lawn. Peter, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Stocks began the week on a down note over inflation fears and the debt ceiling uncertainty. The Dow lost 324, the S&P 500 was off 57. The \uc2 NASDAQ\uc2  dropped 311.\par \par \uc2 What figures to be a monumental term for the \uc2 U.S. Supreme Court\uc2  is now underway. Justices began hearing arguments today on an agenda that will include some huge social issues.\par \par \uc2 Fox News chief legal correspondent, anchor of "FOX NEWS @ NIGHT" Shannon Bream tells us what's on the docket.\par \par \uc2 SHANNON BREAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR (voice-over): For the first time in 18 months, the Supreme Court gathered for in-person arguments Monday in a mostly empty courtroom.\par \par \uc2 Justice Thomas, known for rarely speaking from the bench, dove right in this morning, some say newly confident in his role as the leading voice for the conservative wing. Justice Kavanaugh participated remotely, having tested positive for COVID-19 last week. The term kicking off today includes several potentially landmark cases.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PAUL SMITH, DISTINGUISHED VISITOR FROM PRACTICE, GEORGETOWN UNIVERSITY LAW CENTER: Part of the blockbuster nature of the term will depend on whether they really go very far and say overrule Roe v. Wade or simply narrow it in the abortion case.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: On December 1st, the court will consider Mississippi's law banning most abortions after 15 weeks. Numerous states have passed similar laws hoping to take direct aim at Roe v. Wade.\par \par \uc2 The justices will also re-examine the death penalty for convicted Boston Marathon bomber Dzhokhar Tsarnaev. A lower court throughout the sentence saying the trial judge didn't do enough to protect against jury bias.\par \par \uc2 JONATHAN TURLEY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR (on camera): His attorneys were not allowed to ask prospective jurors about what they watched in the media, and that was viewed by the defense as a real loss to them.\par \par \uc2 BREAM: Guns are also on the dockets. In a challenge to a New York law that requires residents who apply for an application to carry guns in public to show a special need. The plaintiffs were denied their permit requests which they based on self-defense.\par \par \uc2 Gun rights advocates argue the permits should not be reserved only for former law enforcement and high-profile celebrities.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BREAM (on camera): The justices have been notably vocal the last few months. From Justice Breyer warning against plans to pack the court, to Justice Barrett, telling an audience just a few days ago that the court is "not comprised of a bunch of partisan hacks". Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Shannon, thank you. See you tonight.\par \par \uc2 The Biden ministration is reversing a ban on abortion referrals from family planning clinics that lifts a Trump-era restriction. The \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , \uc2 HHS\uc2 , saying its new rules restore the federal family planning program to the way it ran under the Obama administration when clinics were able to refer women seeking abortions to a provider. The change takes effect, November 8th.\par \par \uc2 COVID-19 infections are down by about a third in the past month in the United States. This comes as one major drug makers seeking approval for a pill to treat the virus. And while all of that sounds like positive news, \uc2 Dr. Anthony Fauci\uc2  is sounding a cautionary note. Here is correspondent Steve Harrigan in Atlanta.\par \par \uc2 STEVE HARRIGAN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): As the number of new COVID-19 cases in the U.S. declines down 35 percent since the start of September, the range of options to fight the virus continues to expand.\par \par \uc2 Johnson and Johnson\uc2  will seek authorization this week for a booster. The government is expected to approve a booster shot for the Moderna vaccine following the approval of a \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  booster shot last month, for certain groups including older Americans, those with underlying conditions, and health care workers.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FDA\uc2  is also expected to decide on a \uc2 Pfizer\uc2  vaccine for children aged five to 11 by November. 30,000 children in the U.S. were hospitalized from COVID in August, and the first pill to fight the virus could be available by the end of this year.\par \par \uc2 Merck says its clinical trial of an anti-COVID pill, cut the risk of hospitalization or death from the virus by half. \uc2 Dr. Anthony Fauci\uc2  told "FACE THE NATION", families might not be able to gather for Christmas.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DR. ANTHONY FAUCI\uc2 , CHIEF MEDICAL ADVISOR TO PRESIDENT \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 : It's just too soon to tell. We just got to concentrating on continuing to get those numbers down.\par \par \uc2 HARRIGAN: Today, he tried to clarify his position.\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: I will be spending Christmas with my family. I encourage people, particularly the vaccinated people who are protected to have a good normal Christmas.\par \par \uc2 HARRIGAN: The moves come as teachers in New York City public schools scramble to get vaccinated in response to a mandate that does not allow for a test-out option.\par \par \uc2 Holdouts who have not received a single shot were put on unpaid leave last Friday.\par \par \uc2 STEPHANIE MURPHY, FIFTH GRADE TEACHER: I'm not ready yet. And that's my right as a human being. It's my right as an American to choose when I want to get it.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HARRIGAN: 95 percent of New York City public school teachers have gotten vaccinated. The mayor's response mandates work. Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Steve Harrigan in Atlanta. Steve, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Up next, China continues its aggression toward Taiwan, but blames the U.S.\par \par \uc2 First, here is what some of our Fox affiliates around the country are covering tonight. Fox 11 in Los Angeles, where one of the largest oil spills in recent California history closes beaches, threatens wildlife there. Some people are questioning whether authorities reacted quickly enough to contain that spill.\par \par \uc2 Fox 13 in Tampa as the wife of Florida Governor \uc2 Ron DeSantis\uc2  is diagnosed with breast cancer. His office says Casey DeSantis has his unwavering support, and the prayers and well-wishes from Floridians across the state.\par \par \uc2 And this is a live look at Seattle from Q13 Fox. The big story there tonight. William Shatner, Captain Kirk blasting off into the final frontier next week. The 90-year-old actor who played Captain Kirk in Star Trek will launch into space aboard a Blue Origin capsule. At age 90, Shatner will become the oldest person to fly into space.\par \par \uc2 That is tonight's live look "OUTSIDE THE BELTWAY" from SPECIAL REPORT. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: The first trial of four large pharmacy chains over the opioid epidemic is underway in Cleveland to Ohio counties seek to convince jurors oversight failures at pharmacies run by \uc2 Walgreens Boots Alliance\uc2 , \uc2 CVS Health Corp\uc2 , and \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , as well as \uc2 Giant Eagle\uc2 , lead to excessive amounts of opioid pills flooding their communities.\par \par \uc2 Thousands of similar lawsuits against pharmaceutical companies, drug distributors, and pharmacies are pending.\par \par \uc2 A Florida engineer hiking the Appalachian Trail says he spotted Brian Laundrie early Saturday morning near the North Carolina Tennessee border.\par \par \uc2 Laundrie is a person of interest in the death of girlfriend Gabby Petito.\par \par \uc2 Dennis Davis tells "FOX & FRIENDS" first he encountered a man in a white pickup truck who flashed his lights and waved his hand. David says the man told him he was lost. The man told Davis he was attempting to go to California. David says he notified authorities. The Haywood County, North Carolina Sheriff's Office says deputies did not find Laundrie.\par \par \uc2 Overseas now, the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  says its forces have raided in Islamic State affiliates hideout in the Afghan capital of Kabul and killed several insurgents there. The action occurred hours after a deadly bombing outside a mosque in Kabul. That attack killed five civilians.\par \par \uc2 The bombing was the deadliest incident since the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  took control of Afghanistan after U.S. military withdrawal.\par \par \uc2 China's aggression against Taiwan is accelerating and it's blaming the U.S. Beijing has been sending dozens of fighter planes toward the island nation over the past several days. This comes as the Biden administration tries to decide on a policy to deal with China, both militarily and economically.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent \uc2 Rich Edson\uc2  reports from the White House.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RICH EDSON\uc2 , FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): An aerial show of force from the Chinese military, the largest incursion ever inside Taiwan's air defense zone. 56 planes today, nearly 150 flights since Chinese National Day Friday.\par \par \uc2 China views Taiwan as a breakaway province and Chinese President \uc2 Xi Jinping\uc2  has pledged to bring the island under Chinese Communist Party control.\par \par \uc2 GEN. JACK KEANE (RET.), FOX NEWS NATIONAL SECURITY ANALYST: He said time and time again, we're going to resolve this issue with Taiwan. If it has to be by force, it will be by force. And we're not going to pass this problem on to the next generation.\par \par \uc2 EDSON: The State Department calls China's pressure against Taiwan provocative and destabilizing. \uc2 China's foreign ministry\uc2  blames the U.S. for the tensions, saying "Taiwan belongs to China and the U.S. is in no position to make irresponsible remarks."\par \par \uc2 The United States and its democratic allies are boosting their presence in the region. Four aircraft carriers from the U.S., United Kingdom and Japan began large scale wargames in the western Pacific.\par \par \uc2 The Biden administration is trying to balance a complicated relationship with China, including negotiations on climate change.\par \par \uc2 This morning, U.S. Trade Representative \uc2 Katherine Tai\uc2  announced the Biden administration would initiate new trade negotiations with China, pushing the Chinese government to fulfill promises it made to the Trump administration and accusing China of abusive economic practices.\par \par \uc2 KATHERINE TAI\uc2 , U.S. TRADE REPRESENTATIVE: It is increasingly clear that China's plans do not include meaningful reforms to address the concerns that have been shared by the United States and many other countries.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EDSON (on camera): Tai says the U.S. will maintain tariffs on about $370 billion worth of Chinese imports that the Trump administration implemented, though she says the administration will allow Americans to apply for exemptions from those tariffs, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: \uc2 Rich Edson\uc2  in the White House Briefing Room. Rich, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Up next, we go live to the southern border and we'll talk with the man who just left heading up Border Patrol.\par \par \uc2 First, Beyond our Borders tonight, Russia successfully test-fires new hypersonic missiles from a nuclear submarine for the first time. The \uc2 Russian Defense Ministry\uc2  says two cruise missiles were fired at mock targets. Officials say the missiles will be commissioned by the Russian Navy in 2022.\par \par \uc2 At least 13 people are dead after a strong cyclone sweeps across Oman. Heavy rains triggered landslides and submerged roadways with winds reaching up to 95 miles per hour.\par \par \uc2 Several prominent global figures are denying wrongdoing after a leak of a secret trove of documents about offshore finances. A data dump called the Pandora papers links files to about 35 current and former national leaders and hundreds of other officials. Documents reportedly show the use of offshore accounts to hide wealth from tax collectors and other authorities.\par \par \uc2 The report by the \uc2 International Consortium of Investigative Journalists\uc2  involve 600 journalists from media outlets in 117 countries.\par \par \uc2 Just some of the other stories Beyond our Borders tonight. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Now, to the border crisis. We will talk exclusively with former Border Patrol Chief Rodney Scott over the next two days.\par \par \uc2 First, exclusive new video tonight of our Fox News crew on patrol with Texas State Troopers discovering migrants on the run.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Bill Melugin has tonight's report from La Joya, Texas.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): It's early Monday morning near La Joya, Texas and we are embedded with a Texas State Trooper searching for illegal immigrants hiding in the brush.\par \par \uc2 Within just a matter of minutes, the Trooper and Border Patrol partners were finding migrants seemingly everywhere in one small area near a residential neighborhood.\par \par \uc2 Some of them laying face down in the dirt in an effort to conceal themselves, some wearing camouflage, all of them single adult men or women.\par \par \uc2 The Trooper and Border Agents backed up by a surveillance balloon above called an aerostat, an all-seeing eye providing overwatch during the dark of night.\par \par \uc2 In just a couple of hours, dozens of illegal immigrants were apprehended here, a busy night for border patrol with an assist from Texas DPS.\par \par \uc2 Two weeks ago, as 15,000 Haitians descended on Del Rio, Governor Greg Abbott asked President Biden to declare a federal emergency at the border. The Biden administration refused.\par \par \uc2 And now, Governor Abbott is appealing that decision, saying in part, President Biden has turned his back on Texans living along the border and FEMA's refusal to declare a federal emergency at the border puts their health, safety and property at risk.\par \par \uc2 Former ICE Director Tom Homan says that decision is yet another example of the Biden administration not taking the border seriously.\par \par \uc2 TOM HOMAN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: Biden's proven again to American people that he doesn't believe in border security. The root causes of \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  don't have to go to Central America, she just got to walk down the hall to the Biden administration. There's your root causes, his policies.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN (on camera): And Bret, Panama's Foreign Minister recently warned U.S. officials that there are upwards of 60,000 more Haitian migrants who have moved through Panama and are currently on the way north heading towards the United States.\par \par \uc2 She also pointed out to Texas Congressman Tony Gonzales's office that Panama recently apprehended several people with known ties to Al-Qaeda, as they were also moving north out of Panama.\par \par \uc2 So, some concerning information there. We'll send it back to you.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Hi, Bill, what happened to those people who were caught in the brush last night?\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN: So, for the most part, everybody we saw was a single adult, mostly single adult men. So, what will happen to them is they will likely be expelled from the country via Title 42. That means they'll get put on a bus and just shipped right over to Mexican -- the Mexican side, city of Reynosa. They'll be dropped off, and there's a good chance that some of them will try their luck again, and we could see them out here in these fields once again sometime later on this week.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, great reporting out there. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Former Border Patrol Chief Rodney Scott who just retired in August, told us the threat from illegal immigration is real and serious.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RODNEY SCOTT, FORMER CHIEF, BORDER PATROL: We have nation state threats. We have terrorist threats. We can't get into in this type of a forum, but they're real, they exist and they want to come across that border.\par \par \uc2 Statistically, it always includes rapists, murderers, potential terrorists, every single year. If you look at CBP statistics publicly available, those all exist in who we actually catch.\par \par \uc2 So, to think that there's not just as bad or worse people in those getting away would be naive.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: So, when you hear Secretary Mayorkas said the border is as secured now as it was before, what do you say?\par \par \uc2 SCOTT: That's just not true. And while many of the political appointees assigned currently literally just lack the knowledge and the expertise, that they could make a statement like that and believe that it was true.\par \par \uc2 He's a very smart guy. He's got a lot of experience in Homeland Security. He knows what he's doing. He knows the impacts.\par \par \uc2 I've sat in a room and heard some of the comments he made. He knows what's going on. And he knows that border is not as secure today as it was on January 19th.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: Over the next two days, we will dig deep on the issue of border security, immigration in our exclusive interview with Rodney Scott. Again, just retired in August as the head of Border Patrol. That again is Tuesday and Wednesday on SPECIAL REPORT.\par \par \uc2 Instagram\uc2  and \uc2 Facebook\uc2  and WhatsApp hit by one of their longest ever service outages today, lasting several hours. The companies did not