lemen. Thanks so much. Have a great weekend. When we come back, "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: It's Friday. That means it's time for "Notable Quotables."\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do you think people should, those who call him sleepy Joe should apologize to him?\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: I think we are looking for allowing the president to continue to address multiple crises at a time.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Right now what we are seeing in Texas is frankly chaos. Patients are scared.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This is my first time in my 40 years that I ever saw something like this. I thought Katrina was bad. This is the worst one.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We did not know that the heavens would literally open up and bring Niagara Falls level water to the streets of New York.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: This is tough stuff. War is hard. It's vicious. It's brutal. It's unforgiving.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: They died with their brothers and their sisters right next to them, doing exactly what they all wanted to do.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The war is over, but the heartbreak continues.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The parade of horribles are about to unfold. We are leaving thousands of Afghan allies behind who fought bravely with us.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Do not forget me and my family at the moment in Afghanistan. It is a very hard and horrifying situation.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , (D) PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: Couldn't this have been done in a more orderly manner? I respectfully disagree.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: The White House needs to get some oranges and get tougher with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 PSAKI: We're clearly need to -- sorry, that was aggressive bug.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: Quite a week. Next week on SPECIAL REPORT, we will speak with the education secretary and surgeon general and take some of your questions. That's coming up Thursday. Coming up on FOX NEWS SUNDAY, Congressman Michael McCaul and \uc2 Dr. Ashish Jha\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Thank you for watching SPECIAL REPORT. FOX NEWS PRIMETIME hosted by Tammy Bruce starts right now. Have a wonderful Labor Day weekend and great show, Tammy.\par \par \uc2 TAMMY BRUCE, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Thank you, sir. Nice to see you, Mike. And good evening, everyone, and welcome to FOX NEWS PRIMETIME.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020210904eh9300001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Biden Admin Spins Afghan Withdrawal Catastrophe; Military Leaders More Focused On CRT Than Winning; Dems Ignore Slain Troops To Attack Conservatives; U.S. Program from Allowing Refugees from Afghanistan to Emigrate to U.S. Examined; Land Given to Veterans Housing in Southern California Largely Unoccupied by Homeless Veterans Due to Veterans Administration\b0\par\par\uc2 Raymond Arroyo, Jason Chaffetz \par \uc2 7,337 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 September 2021\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2021 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2021 ASC Services II Media, LLC. All materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast without the prior written permission of ASC Services II Media, LLC. You may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY, FOX NEWS HOST: But let not your heart be troubled.\par \par \uc2 Ray Arroyo filling in for Laura tonight. Ray, how are you, sir?\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS HOST: Thank you, Sean. I'm a little froggy tonight. Listen to this.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: What happened to your voice?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I don't know. But we'll handle through.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: You're filling in for Laura and you got a sore throat. I'm sorry.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Typical.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: It sounds - let me guess, it sounds worse than you feel.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes. I feel great. We'll get through.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: OK. By the way, it happens to me. Anytime I get any sickness, it goes right for the vocal cords. Hang in there, my friend. I've been there.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Thank you. I'm Raymond Arroyo in for Laura Ingraham tonight. This is the "Ingraham Angle" from New York City.\par \par \uc2 Forgive this. Tonight, as we bring you Afghan refugees by the thousands, a similar number of American veterans are languishing in our streets. An exclusive report from LA will break your heart. Also, as media and political heads explode over the Texas heartbeat bill withstanding a Supreme Court challenge, Texas lieutenant governor Dan Patrick is here to give us his reaction to the uproar.\par \par \uc2 And while the Biden administration plays patty-cake with the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 , Lara Logan will tell us exactly who they are legitimising. But first, you probably have to go back to [ph] punches pilot to find a public official more committed to absolving himself of culpability for his actions, while throwing out shiny objects to distract people.\par \par \uc2 President Biden and his administration are laboring to offshore responsibility for the loss of life in Afghanistan, and the abandonment of Americans there.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 GEORGE STEPHANOPOULOS, ABC NEWS HOST: So Americans should understand the troops might have to be there beyond August 31.\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT, UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: And if you're American force, if there's American citizens left, we're going to stay till we get them all out.\par \par \uc2 The bottom line, 90 percent of Americans in Afghanistan who wanted to leave were able to leave.\par \par \uc2 JOHN KIRBY, PENTAGON PRESS SECRETARY: I mean, we have Americans that get stranded in countries all the time.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Meanwhile, the Biden Defense Department is focused on critical race theory. And the Deputy Defense Secretary in an op-ed is turning her attention not to bringing Americans home, but to addressing racial disparities in the military justice system.\par \par \uc2 Congress is holding hearings on terrorism this week. Oh, not about the people who killed our servicemen in Afghanistan. Forget about them. There are bigger threats among us.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. BENNIE THOMPSON (D-MS): It was an international terrorist threat. If we talk to our intelligence bureau agencies now, they are telling us that their threat landscape is now a more of a domestic nature.\par \par \uc2 DANIEL BYMAN, GEORGETOWN UNIVERSITY PROFESSOR: Today, in the United States, the right wing and white supremacist's violence is a much greater risk.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: These are partisans utterly detached from reality. They're doing everything they can to avoid responsibility for the real carnage in our midst, and avoid Americans questions about their culpability.\par \par \uc2 The other night, Laura spoke with Paula Knauss. She's the mother of the military hero slain in Afghanistan last week.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 PAULA KNAUSS, MOTHER OF STAFF SGT RYAN KNAUSS: If Mr. Biden would like to tell me how I can sleep better at night right now, or any American can while he is serving in administration. Please give me a call.\par \par \uc2 We are in Congress, we are in our nation's capitol. Who will stand up and say, I messed up? I am responsible. Who will do that?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Not Biden, nor his party. They don't give a damn. They're content to compound that woman's pain with their silence and pretend they're not responsible. And now, we're even trying to strike all memory of these men, these slain men and women from the public record.\par \par \uc2 On Tuesday, a group of Republican vets tried to read the names of our 13 American heroes into the Congressional Record. Congresswoman Debbie Dingell and the Democrat leadership gaveled the House out of session and shut down their request.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. DEBBIE DINGELL (D-MI): The House stands adjourned until noon on Friday, September 3, 2021.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: The People's House, the only conversation someone have about Afghanistan is about importing half the country here.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Let's hope that our commitment to refugees who helped our country has not been forgotten.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: America has always been the country that opens our heart.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Every Afghan who is interested in doing so should be given asylum inside the United States.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Do you know what did this cost the American taxpayer? The look over caucus doesn't want you thinking about that. Now, politicians and the media have found a new shiny object to draw your attention when floods swept away homes in Tennessee last week, it barely registered in the media.\par \par \uc2 This week when Ida wiped out thousands of homes and shut down power for millions of people, including in my city of New Orleans, the national media shrugged. But when Ida's remnants hit New York and New Jersey last night, it suddenly harm again [ph] Noah on Broadway.\par \par \uc2 After trying all night to avoid the Afghanistan disaster, CNN found a story in light and Brian Stelter became a storm chaser.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: It's just crazy in from New York City so unprecedented.\par \par \uc2 BRIAN STELTER, CNN HOST: I think the volume, the velocity as you were talking about the amount of rainwater coming down in the span of an hour or two overwhelms the infrastructure.\par \par \uc2 JOHN BERMAN, CNN HOST: Where I live, the rain was just torrential. When I left my house this morning, a while ago now, I mean, there was a giant tree on the street. This is a site you don't think you're going to see which is a tree down blocking the road.\par \par \uc2 JOHN AVLON, CNN POLITICAL ANALYST: It is being overwhelmed by the climate crisis. And there needs to be massive investment to mitigate this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Well, at least they're covering American suffering. And our hearts are with all our friends, not only here in the east, but deep south back home, suffering from Ida. And you can always count on the look over here caucus not to let tragedy go to waste.\par \par \uc2 The people responsible for Afghanistan, the COVID shutdowns, and inflation, go right to the playbook. Note, the coordinated language.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. CHUCK SCHUMER (D-NY): Woe is us, if we don't recognize these changes are due to climate change. Woe is us, if we don't do something about it quickly, both in building resilient infrastructure and going to clean power.\par \par \uc2 GOV. PHIL MURPHY (D-NJ): A lot of it will be put into resilient infrastructure. Any amount of investment we can make in the years ahead in resilient infrastructure will be investment that will help us.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yes. Stick to