ere this therapeutic culture caught all, it started where I work in the university. But it's not the tragic view of the world that George Marshall and George Patton and Admiral Nimitz once held. They were different breed than the current military establishment.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Victor, I thank you for being here. With this voice, I'm going to step aside and Jason is going to take over for the evening. So Jason, thank you. And I'll be back next week.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Thanks, Raymond. And get better. Hope you feel better. I do appreciate it.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: I feel fine. It's just the voice.\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: Yes. You look fine. It just - you have the voice. I get it. We've all been there. We've all been there. See you around.\par \par \uc2 All right. Is Biden on track to legitimize the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 ? Lara Logan is here on the \uc2 Taliban\uc2  (inaudible) and what he could mean to our security. Plus, what's the price tag of playing - paying for all those refugees for the rest of their lives? Kash Patel breaks down what taxpayers could be on the hook for. Stay tuned.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CHAFFETZ: All right. Now, that was actually a really good show. And I'm old enough to remember that show. So are you ready to meet our new best friends in America? Because they're - they enjoy growing beards, selling opium, enforcing Sharia law, and they recently acquired their own Airforce, courtesy of you, the American people. That's right. It's the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 . Here's team Biden in their own words.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: What is the \uc2 Taliban\uc2 ? Are they now our frenemy?\par \par \uc2 Well, it's hard to put a label on it. In part because we have yet to see what they are going to be now that they are in control.\par \par \uc2 GENERAL MARK MILLEY, CHAIRMAN OF THE JOINT CHIEFS OF STAFF: In war, you do what you must in order to reduce risk.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Any 