he law signed by Republican Governor Greg Abbott bans abortion once a so-called fetal heartbeat is detected, usually around six weeks.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: How is an abortion service different from abortion? Why not just call it what it is. But here's the best line from CBS, "a so-called fetal heartbeat." Imagine saying something like that out loud.\par \par \uc2 Once they've decided you should die, they won't even admit you have a heartbeat. Do the very worst people in this country go into journalism or does it just seem that way?\par \par \uc2 Anyway, you'll notice that CBS does not make a case for abortion. No. They didn't tell you why it's so important to stop fetal hearts from beating. They just asserted that it is.\par \par \uc2 What they didn't do is say a single word of how this violates your physical autonomy, about how it's your body your choice. They can't say that now. They are for mandating vaccines and masks.\par \par \uc2 So in that way over at CBS, they are still a little bit smarter than the protesters you're seeing on your screen right now. These are the people who gathered outside the Texas State Capitol in Austin today. You'll notice that many of them are holding signs affirming their physical autonomy. You can't tell them what to do with their bodies. Politicians, hands off my body.\par \par \uc2 But wait a second, at the very same moment they're declaring their physical autonomy, they are wearing their little obedience masks and you can bet money all of them are vaccinated. Why? Because they were told to get the shot, so of course they obeyed.\par \par \uc2 They don't see the irony here. On the other hand, how could they see it?\par \par \uc2 So few sane people are left with big platforms in this country that you almost never hear a sensible logical rational argument about anything.\par \par \uc2 Just hours ago, for example, the ACLU, \uc2 the American Civil Liberties Union\uc2  released this statement and we're