ng likely voters.\par \par \uc2 NEWSOM: Polls don`t vote, people vote.\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: Of 22 million ballots mailed out, voters returned one in five. The recall ballot has two questions. One, should Newsome be recalled? Two, who should replace him?\par \par \uc2 Well, that second question won`t matter if Newsome wins a majority on the first. Conservative radio host Larry Elder leads the challengers.\par \par \uc2 LARRY ELDER (R), GUBERNATORIAL CANDIDATE, CALIFORNIA: I urge you all to vote to recall \uc2 Gavin Newsom\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: Elder is facing an avalanche of negative media coverage following 20 years of provocative radio commentary. Along with allegations, he once use, a racial slur during a comedy sketch, and that he pulled a weapon on an ex-fiancee while high on pot.\par \par \uc2 ELDER: This is not the first time the L.A. Times has attacked me. There`s another writer who also called me a black \uc2 David Duke\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: Newsom`s big advantage, bags of cash from unions and liberal donors to dominate the airwaves.\par \par \uc2 SEN. BERNIE SANDERS (D-VT): The last thing we need is to have some right- wing Republican governor in California.\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE: Yet, state Democrats are nervous. Instead of a booming economy following COVID rates and schools back to normal, Newsome faces raging fires, angry parents, rising crime, and a homeless epidemic.\par \par \uc2 ELDER: They are scared to death. They know that if California can elect a conservative governor like myself, and they can, and they will on September the 14th, that any state can.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 LA JEUNESSE (on camera): While this latest poll shows Republicans more motivated than Democrats, they outnumber the GOP two to one.\par \par \uc2 But Latino voters who have long favored Democrats could make a difference. Republicans believe, despite the polls, that they`ve lost confidence in Governor Newsome, was bringing in Senator Elizabeth Warren this weekend to campaign here in California. Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, William, thank you. More on this with the panel.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 Federal Aviation Administration\uc2  says Virgin Galactic cannot launch anyone into space again until an investigation is complete into a mishap during July`s flight with founder \uc2 Richard Branson\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 FAA\uc2  says the ship carrying Branson and five Virgin Galactic employees veered off course during its descent back to New Mexico. The deviation put the ship outside the air traffic control clearance area.\par \par \uc2 The ban comes is Virgin Galactic announces plans to launch three Italian researchers to the edge of space in just a few weeks.\par \par \uc2 Up next, the broken promises on Afghanistan. We`ll look at some of the criticism hounding President Biden.\par \par \uc2 Plus a bird`s eye view of Ida`s wrath in Louisiana.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: President Biden is facing increasing criticism tonight for what some critics say is clearly a broken promise about getting Americans and thousands of Afghans who helped America out of Afghanistan.\par \par \uc2 White House correspondent Peter Doocy looks at the controversy tonight.\par \par \uc2 PETER DOOCY, FOX NEWS WHITE HOUSE CORRESPONDENT (voice-over): Afghanistan policy has not played out as advertised.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 JOE BIDEN\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: If there`s American citizens left, we`re going to stay and we will get them all out.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Turns out all out meant nine out of 10.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: 90 percent of Americans in Afghanistan who wanted to leave were able to leave.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: So, even though the administration initially claimed --\par \par \uc2 JEN PSAKI\uc2 , WHITE HOUSE PRESS SECRETARY: It`s irresponsible to say Americans are stranded. They are not.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: The Pentagon later clarified