his is \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  calls an extraordinary success. He says it was the right decision, the wise decision, the best decision, unparalleled results. Wow.\par \par \uc2 And then he went on to say, what a magnificent display of public policy. I ask again, if that's success, how do we define failure?\par \par \uc2 Because today, \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  took again zero questions. He was exhausted from yesterday. He's yelling at us and lecturing of us, and he apparently wants to move past his Afghan debacle. This crisis is not over.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, the war is not over either. Americans are held hostage, right now, behind enemy lines.\par \par \uc2 And even today, "The Washington Post" reported that a hundred \uc2 U.S. government\uc2 -sponsored journalists and their families all left behind by \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  in Afghanistan. There are now hundreds and hundreds maybe more than a thousand Americans with no way out and, of course, we have no update on the exact number or their whereabouts. No concrete plan at all to rescue them.\par \par \uc2 We have no diplomats on the ground. We have no military on the ground. No accurate accounting even of how many Americans are behind enemy lines. This is unforgivable.\par \par \uc2 These Americans have been left behind and abandoned by their president. I never thought I'd see this in my lifetime.\par \par \uc2 You know, I thought you didn't leave people behind, Joe. You said it over and over and over again. We don't leave people behind you said it two weeks ago, Joe. You promised over and over again, in case you forgot, which is probably highly likely.\par \par \uc2 Take a look.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: If there's American citizens left, we're going to stay and we get them all out.\par \par \uc2 This town, this state, this country takes care of our own, leaves nobody behind.\par \par \uc2 Giving anyone a fair shot, leaving nobody behind.\par \par \uc2 That we do take care of our own, that 