g, David.\par \par \uc2 DAVID LEE MILLER, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (on camera): Bret, even after his resignation takes effect. Governor Cuomo's legal problems are only likely just beginning.\par \par \uc2 MILLER (voice-over): Multiple investigations on the state and federal level could result in fines, the payout of monetary damages, and even the possibility of time behind bars. Prosecutors in at least four New York counties are looking into whether Cuomo's alleged sexual harassment was criminal.\par \par \uc2 One of the women, Brittany Commisso has already filed a criminal complaint in Albany County, which is the home of the state capitol. The Albany County Sheriff issued a statement soon after Cuomo went public with his planned resignation, saying in part, "Today's announcement will have no effect on our investigation. We still have a complaint and an allegation of criminal conduct. Our investigation continues."\par \par \uc2 Unlike the investigation by the state attorney general that sparked Cuomo's resignation, a criminal conviction would have to meet the higher standard of guilt beyond a reasonable doubt.\par \par \uc2 According to a former New York prosecutor, a possible charge of forcible touching is not a felony in New York State.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RANDY ZELIN, FORMER NEW YORK STATE PROSECUTOR: That could be argued as unfair, as outrageous as -- how can it only be a misdemeanor? Well, again, a misdemeanor still carries up to a year in jail. It still carries up to three years of probation, and it carries a criminal record.\par \par \uc2 So, let's not water down the seriousness of being convicted of a misdemeanor sex offense.\par \par \uc2 MILLER: Cuomo could also face possible prison time resulting from a federal investigation into his administration's handling of COVID nursing home deaths if charged with obstruction of justice.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MILLER (on camera): State investigators, meanwhile, 