-described socialist colleague, Chairman Sanders.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: The president is also trying to figure out how to get more people vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: And I understand that to badger those folks is not likely to get them to move and get vaccinated.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: And has lawyers looking to see if you can intervene in states that don't enforce mask mandates.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: We're checking that but there are -- on federal workforce, I can.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: The feds were reportedly considering withholding funds from Florida.\par \par \uc2 PSAKI: Obviously, we don't want to hurt the people of Florida.\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: But today, the president focus less on the pandemic and more on a victory lap.\par \par \uc2 BIDEN: I know a lot of people, some sitting in the audience here didn't think this could happen. This bill's declared dead more often than anyway.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DOOCY (on camera): The president doesn't usually host an event like that until there is a bill to sign and there's not right now. This infrastructure package has only passed the Senate, not the House.\par \par \uc2 He did use his remarks, though, to talk up the value of bipartisanship, which was definitely on display with infrastructure. But bipartisanship is not expected to be part of the next package, Bret.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: And Peter, even though across the country there are these talks about vaccine mandates underway, there's still no one nominated to head the \uc2 FDA\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 DOOCY: Right and there still is no \uc2 FDA\uc2  final authorization full approval of the vaccines. But the president says -- said today he understands that is something that is driving vaccine hesitancy and even though the vaccination stats have been improving recently, he sees this final \uc2 FDA\uc2  approval as something that is going to get the numbers even higher. And he says he hopes it comes in the next couple of weeks, Bret.\par \par \uc2 