ke that? Well, that's the level of public conversation.\par \par \uc2 STEYN: Well, exactly and I said that, you know, you laugh at this and I laugh at this, you know the people who really laugh at this, Chairman Xi and the Chinese politburo, because they don't have to bother thinking about any of this and it frees up all the remarkable amount of time to talk about something important and something true.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, that's so nicely put, as always, Mark Steyn, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 STEYN: Thanks a lot, Tucker.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So obviously, there's a lot going on. We've got a revolution in progress. How should people who aren't kind of with the program, respond to this? We try to find people who thought deeply about this question because it's interesting and all of a sudden important.\par \par \uc2 After the break, we'll share a conversation we had with one of them.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Ted Lieu is a Member of Congress. He is a Democrat who represents the State of California. He's incredibly smart. He went to Stanford and Georgetown. So when Ted Lieu speaks, you're really seeing the Democratic Party's brain trust on display. With that in mind, we wanted to bring you one of his recent pronouncements. This is a tweet and it's in response to one of his colleagues, the Congressman Scott Perry.\par \par \uc2 Now Perry was making an argument we have often made because it's true and that is that Democrats are using mass immigration to transform the country to change who votes so they can control who wins.\par \par \uc2 Ted Lieu was very annoyed that Scott Perry said this and so he sent the following tweet, and he was clearly enraged as he did, quote: "Dear Scott Perry, native-born Americans like you are no more American and no less American than an immigrant like me." Good point. We agree with that.\par \par \uc2 And then he said this, "And with every passing year, there will be more people who look like m