ic fundamental principles on which this country was founded, if the people decide that the government is no longer protecting their rights, they have both a right and a duty, which is interesting to alter or abolish that government and replace it with something that they think will serve what the declaration calls their safety and happiness.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: I don't think you could post that on \uc2 Twitter\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 ELLMERS: It's hate speech, right? Isn't it hate speech?\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Well, it's a massive and glaring threat of course to the rent seekers now running everything.\par \par \uc2 ELLMERS: Right.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: Declaration of Independence as hate speech. Barely an overstatement.\par \par \uc2 The full conversation with Glenn Ellmers on "Tucker Carlson Today." You can find it on foxnation.com, Monday, Wednesday and Friday are the days it comes out. Stream at any time. It's not hard.\par \par \uc2 So you're hearing from the Biden administration, they are never going to require vaccine passports, ever. Of course, vaccine passports are coming. In some cases, they're on the way. It'll be their proxies, not them requiring them.\par \par \uc2 It turns out the most powerful corporations in the country have been building digital databases on your health. Kind of a remarkable story. Details straight ahead.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So we're not getting vaccine passports, Joe Biden has assured, you know, instead, the most powerful corporations in the world are going to provide vaccine passports and mandate their use, so if you don't have a passport to prove you've been vaccinated, even if you have antibodies from a natural infection, well, you can't live here.\par \par \uc2 Mastercard\uc2  and the \uc2 International Chamber of Commerce\uc2  have announced the partnership on vaccine passports, companies like \uc2 Walmart\uc2 , \uc2 IBM\uc2  and \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  are workin