c2  take a lie detector test? What about all of the I-believers in the Democratic Party? They have been silent lately.\par \par \uc2 You might remember some of them.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES: I believe her. Listen, first of all, anybody who comes forward at this point to be prepared to testify in the \uc2 United States Senate\uc2  against someone who is being nominated to one of the most powerful positions in the \uc2 United States government\uc2 , that takes an extraordinary amount of courage.\par \par \uc2 SEN. MAZIE HIRONO (D-HI): Not only do women like Dr. Ford who bravely comes forward need to be heard, but they need to be believed. They need to be believed.\par \par \uc2 SEN. RICHARD BLUMENTHAL (D-CT): Let me say at the outset, I believe Dr. Ford. I believe the survivor here.\par \par \uc2 SEN. KIRSEN GILLIBRAND (D-NY): I believe her. I stand with her.\par \par \uc2 SEN. CHUCK SCHUMER (D-NY): I believe Professor Ford. I think she's credible. And I think when the investigation is finished and when she testifies and Judge Kavanaugh testifies, I think a majority of senators will find her credible.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: So, tonight, we are asking, where are all of you I-believers now? Because none of the people we just showed you that you saw with your own eyes, none of them have yet come forward with statement saying, they believe Cuomo's accusers. Not one. And not Cuomo himself.\par \par \uc2 Perhaps the biggest I-believer of them all, well, was then Senator \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . Remember? She frequently praised the courage of Kavanaugh's accusers.\par \par \uc2 Well, tonight, here's what the now Vice President Harris has to say about Cuomo's accuser. Take a look.\par \par \uc2 Oh, crickets. Vice President Harris, where are you? Coming in, Vice President Harris? Where is your brave leadership on this important subject today?\par \par \uc2 I was one of