oesn't know what to do.\par \par \uc2 So, I think a lot of people tonight are saying, of course, we believe that we should follow the due process of law. But it is -- it is sort of something that feels like now you see how we felt when Christine Blasey Ford arrived after 30 years of amnesia, set that up with 30 years of amnesia with absolutely zero proof and went after \uc2 Brett Kavanaugh\uc2 . And we were told, you have to #believe women. You have to #metoo, absent any facts.\par \par \uc2 So it's really hard for me to find in my heart to feel bad for Governor Cuomo tonight.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: But, you know, if you really do believe in the concept of the presumption of innocence and due process, that's a little bit harder. You know, I can give you a litany, a long list Candace of issues where we got things right and the media mob got things wrong. We were right about Russia, the hoax, the conspiracy theories, the lies, the misinformation.\par \par \uc2 This program, I started out in Atlanta, Georgia. I was right about Richard Jewel. I didn't rush to judgment. UVA, we were right there. Duke lacrosse, we were right there. We were right on Ferguson and we were right on Baltimore and we were right on Cambridge. And the media, they get it wrong all the time.\par \par \uc2 Sometimes, it might take me a little longer to get to the answer, but I'm going to wait and see what the evidence shows us. But they're not willing to do that to conservatives but they give every bit of due process and total silence for their fellow Democrats.\par \par \uc2 And we shouldn't be surprised about that. I mean, you bring up \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 . This is a woman that stood on stage next to \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  and called him a racist. She called him out on his policies which he -- she was accurate in that assumption, by the way, calling him out on his -- on his voting record back when he was senator and said, I was that little girl.\par \par \uc2 And what did she do? She then strapped