2 LEVINE: Senator, transgender medicine is a very complexed and nuanced field. If confirmed to the position of assistant secretary of health, I would certainly be pleased to come to your office and talk with you and your staff.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: Here with reaction, FOX News contributor, Rachel Campos-Duffy, and author of "Panic Attack", Dr. Nicole Saphier.\par \par \uc2 All right. Dr. Sapphire, you are a medical doctor. This is a life-changing event. The question is about parents and whether or not they have a right to be informed of these decisions. Thoughts?\par \par \uc2 DR. NICOLE SAPHIER, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: That's right, Sean. It's important to clarify the question I wasn't about transgender in general. It was about minors and being transgender.\par \par \uc2 And my biggest concern with some of the treatments that are going on for children that are identifying as transgender is I don't want a life-long identity to be defined by childhood insecurities. The biggest concern I have as a mother and as a physician, puberty is a fundamental psychological development as well as the frontal lobe is not fully developed until the mid-20s.\par \par \uc2 And that's really where your decision making and your reasoning comes from. I have a hard time doing anything permanent in terms of hormone and surgery that until a child has been fully developed. That is my biggest concern.\par \par \uc2 HANNITY: And, Rachel, your take on that.\par \par \uc2 RACHEL CAMPOS-DUFFY, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Listen, Dr. Levine is a pediatrician. The most important attribute of a pediatrician is that they love and care about children. People who want to normalize changing the sex of children and not letting their parents who are the best people to care for them know about it are people who don't care about children.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, we shouldn't be surprised. We've seen adults willing to put their political agenda ahead of children all year long in