some way, at great expense to yourself. So thank you for doing that. Thanks for coming on tonight.\par \par \uc2 SHRIER: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: So it's been a pretty heavy show. Sorry about that. We tried to lighten it up at some point, it is a little relentless. Tonight, it certainly was. So we're going to end with this.\par \par \uc2 Rod Ponton is county attorney in Presidio County, Texas, and today, he had a little difficulty during a virtual hearing before a Texas District Court Judge. Here's what happened.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JUDGE ROY FERGUSON, PRESIDIO COUNTY, TEXAS: Mr. Ponton, I believe you have a filter turned on in the video settings. You might want to find out.\par \par \uc2 ROD PONTON, COUNTY ATTORNEY, PRESIDIO COUNTY, TEXAS: Can you hear me, Judge?\par \par \uc2 FERGUSON: I can hear you. I think it's a filter it and --\par \par \uc2 PONTON: It is and I don't know how to remove it. I've got my assistant here, she is trying to, but I'm prepared to go forward with it. I'm here live. It's not that -- I'm not a cat.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: "I am not a cat." Probably the best line ever from a lawyer in American history, "I am not a cat." He took it well in the end.\par \par \uc2 The lawyer told reporters quote: "If I can make the country chuckle for a moment in these difficult times they're going through, I'm happy to let them do that at my expense." In other words, the American spirit is not dead. It's just slightly more feline than normal. We appreciate that.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for joining us tonight. We'll be back tomorrow and every night at 8:00 p.m. The show that is the sworn enemy of lying pomposity, smugness and groupthink.\par \par \uc2 Buckle up, it's going to get better.\par \par \uc2 In the meantime, Sean Hannity takes over 9:00 p.m. right now.\par \par \uc2 SEAN HANNITY, FOX NEWS CHANNEL HOST: The cat is a star. That's all there is to it.\par \par \uc2 CARLSON: It was good.\par